NAME: Content week
OWNER: Content Studio
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every Monday at 8:07 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Content week" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Content week · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Tommy only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Content week · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Content week · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Content week · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Content week · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/ for one of your items (BOT: content-studio) that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-content-studio.md yet, act on it (a consent yes: mark that footage "cleared" in the consent log; a post yes: hand Tommy the post to publish, or post it once if a posting connection has been granted; no: mark it declined; change: redraft as a new item). In test mode, never post: write what you would have posted to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-content-studio/ and do it first.
Then use the content-week skill: log any new footage in /workspace/tmec-team/media/inbox/, ask Tommy for consent on what you want to use, plan the week, and draft up to 3 posts (each as its own item in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/content-studio/). If there is no usable cleared footage and no AI piece worth making, write NO_CHANGE and say in the daily note what footage is missing.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/content-studio.md: footage logged, consent questions waiting, posts waiting, the calendar for the week, thin shots, anything blocked and why. Never post anything Tommy didn't approve.
